{"ts":"2026-08-25T05:15:02.078Z","author":"harness:codex","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-5.6-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"9b054e739855a3b67742faac","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-5.6-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-2ga1g7","claim:pm-a8zm","lineage:pm-2ga1g7","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-2ga1g7+pm-a8zm","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-2ga1g7","claim:pm-a8zm","lineage:pm-2ga1g7","lineage:pm-doxj"]}},"op":"update","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/body","value":"## Failure boundary\n\nThe tracker-mode linked-test sandbox copies or derives non-trivial workspace settings and must record the exact final settings document in the workspace history stream. The current seeding path writes a settings history event whose replayed document is empty, so strict history-drift validation correctly rejects the sandbox.\n\n## Repair constraints\n\n- Preserve sandbox isolation and never read or write the real project tracker during the linked command.\n- Build the final settings document once and use that same value for disk persistence and the immutable workspace history event.\n- Cover default and non-trivial settings, schema and tracker context modes, nested strict validation, repeated seeding, and deterministic replay.\n- Add a negative control that restores the empty history document and proves the gate fails."},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-25T05:15:02.078Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags/0","value":"history-integrity"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags/1","value":"linked-tests"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags/2","value":"regression"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags/3","value":"tracker-context"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":240},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"The tracker sandbox writes byte-equivalent final settings content to settings.json and the authoritative workspace history event; Nested validate --check-history-drift --strict-exit passes for non-trivial tracker-mode settings; Schema mode remains isolated and behavior-compatible; Repeated seeding is deterministic and does not duplicate or reorder history unexpectedly; A negative control with an empty replay document fails the exact strict history gate"}],"before_hash":"db33c87cd178bcbfce16af7360b95cd4009de76a625aa801ac3794bb7c9c50db","after_hash":"ec761770ea4b105e0b624b95185f19566eb686289b44e52bdfda18cb4cd4b82f","item_hash_version":2,"message":"Complete the only active acceptance-criteria and estimate gap found by the all-status census","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}}}
